    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <p>Simplified reversible five-reaction O2 model of the authors&apos; heat-map script, which reproduces Fig. 11 of the article: <strong>Selective oxidation of 3-hydroxypropionic acid to malonic acid over Pd/C: Mechanistic and kinetic study.</strong> Kim S.Y., Chavarrio J.E., Install J., Huber G.W. <i>Appl. Catal. B: Environ. Energy</i> 386 (2026) 126403. DOI: <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apcatb.2026.126403">10.1016/j.apcatb.2026.126403</a></p>
        <p>Transcribed from the authors&apos; script APCATB_D_25_08770_heatmap.m (Dryad, DOI 10.5061/dryad.jsxksn0q4). This is not the Table 3 / Fig. 9b model: there is no OPA intermediate and every step has a reverse term. The model is not written out in the paper. </p>
        <p>Default state: the constant set that reproduces Fig. 11b, at 50 C, with the heat-map initial condition (unit mole fractions; x_per_M = 1/C0). The rate constants k_1, k_2 and k_5 come from the deposited Arrhenius table (11-4_Arrhenius.csv), the equilibrium constants from the script&apos;s printed starting vector, and k_3 and k_4 were inferred from the contour lines of the published figure; the fitted values themselves were not deposited. The Arrhenius factors are applied to the rate constants and to the equilibrium constants, as in the script. </p>
      </body>
